    "body": "Hmm, I can maybe sign up for that. Let's first discuss the exact behavior.\n\nI'm struggling a bit with the proposed behavior for the density scenarios. I find it really ungainly that for a 2x-density-known-width-only case we render 150 height but report 75 height intrinsic. I understand that we cannot return 0 now and that null (my preferred solution) is thus also out of the question. I also understand from Elika that rendering 75 for 2x-density is not really seen as an option. (And arguably it's a bit weird as density is completely unrelated to replaced elements.)\n\nBut how about we just do the same thing as CSS? If the intrinsic height and intrinsic aspect ratio are unknown, we return 150 for `naturalHeight`. And vice versa for `naturalWidth`. (And if we add `naturalAspectRatio` we do return null for the unknown case.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
